      "rkaf:fragmentContentDigest": "sha256:668999c51c74d480383126ed520172cea18a50cba1239cdc7337af5ed0e7a425",
      "rkaf:selectorKind": [
        "oa:TextQuoteSelector",
        "oa:TextPositionSelector"
      ],
      "oa:hasSelector": [
        {
          "@type": "oa:TextQuoteSelector",
          "oa:exact": "(4) Nothing in this section prevents employers from considering employment prior to a continuous break in service of more than seven years when determining whether an employee has met the 12-month employment requirement. However, if an employer chooses to recognize such prior employment, the employer must do so uniformly, with respect to all employees with similar breaks in service."
        },
        {
          "@type": "oa:TextPositionSelector",
          "oa:start": 2419,
          "oa:end": 2804,
          "rkaf:coordinateSystem": "rkaf:unicode-codepoint"
        }
      ]
    },
